@page "/"

<PageTitle>Clarity Belongs - Keep an eye on what matters</PageTitle>

<div class="shell public-shell">
    <section class="public-hero public-hero-grid">
        <div class="hero-copy">
            <div class="eyebrow">CLARITY BELONGS</div>
            <h1>Tell Clarity what matters. We keep an eye on it.</h1>
            <p class="public-lead">Public websites, endpoints, domains, certificates, DNS records, and service status sources. Clarity checks them over time, remembers what it saw, and shows you when the observed state changes.</p>
            <div class="action-row public-actions">
                <AuthorizeView>
                    <Authorized>
                        <a class="button" href="/add">Watch something</a>
                        <a class="button secondary" href="/my-clarity">Open My Clarity</a>
                    </Authorized>
                    <NotAuthorized>
                        <a class="button" href="/signup">Start free</a>
                        <a class="button secondary" href="/products">See what Clarity can watch</a>
                    </NotAuthorized>
                </AuthorizeView>
            </div>
            <p class="microcopy">Start with five things for free. No card required.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="hero-visual" aria-label="Example Clarity activity">
            <div class="hero-visual-topline">
                <span class="status-dot"></span>
                <span>Clarity is watching</span>
                <span class="hero-live-pill">Live</span>
            </div>
            <div class="hero-watch-card hero-watch-card-featured">
                <div class="watch-icon">↗</div>
                <div>
                    <small>Observed state changed</small>
                    <strong>Webpage content changed</strong>
                    <span>Before and after saved</span>
                </div>
                <span class="watch-state changed">Changed</span>
            </div>
            <div class="hero-watch-card">
                <div class="watch-icon">✓</div>
                <div>
                    <small>Still responding</small>
                    <strong>softwarebelongs.com</strong>
                    <span>Checked 2 minutes ago</span>
                </div>
                <span class="watch-state healthy">Healthy</span>
            </div>
            <div class="hero-watch-card">
                <div class="watch-icon">◷</div>
                <div>
                    <small>Expiration approaching</small>
                    <strong>Certificate renewal</strong>
                    <span>14 days remaining</span>
                </div>
                <span class="watch-state reminder">Reminder</span>
            </div>
            <p>One place to review checks and history instead of reopening the same sources yourself.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="public-section idea-section">
        <div class="section-intro">
            <div class="eyebrow">HOW IT WORKS</div>
            <h2>You choose the target. Clarity handles the repeated checks.</h2>
            <p>Pick a direct monitoring capability, give Clarity the public target, and it records observations and history using the matching monitor underneath.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-grid">
            <div><strong>1</strong><span>Choose a target</span></div>
            <div><strong>2</strong><span>Clarity checks it</span></div>
            <div><strong>3</strong><span>History builds</span></div>
            <div><strong>4</strong><span>Review detected changes</span></div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="public-section monitor-section">
        <div class="section-heading">
            <div>
                <div class="eyebrow">WHAT CAN CLARITY WATCH?</div>
                <h2>Start with direct monitoring capabilities.</h2>
            </div>
            <a href="/products">Browse all public capabilities</a>
        </div>
        <div class="product-grid public-product-grid">
            <a class="product-card monitor-card" href="/products/website-uptime">
                <div class="monitor-icon">◎</div>
                <div class="eyebrow">WEBSITE AVAILABILITY</div>
                <h2>Websites and endpoints</h2>
                <p>Monitor uptime, HTTP status, redirects, broken links, API endpoints, and public service endpoints.</p>
                <span class="monitor-link">See availability monitors →</span>
            </a>
            <a class="product-card monitor-card" href="/products/ssl-expiration">
                <div class="monitor-icon">◷</div>
                <div class="eyebrow">DOMAIN & CERTIFICATE</div>
                <h2>Domains and SSL certificates</h2>
                <p>Track certificate identity and expiration plus public domain-registry expiration data.</p>
                <span class="monitor-link">See domain monitors →</span>
            </a>
            <a class="product-card monitor-card" href="/products/dns-change">
                <div class="monitor-icon">↗</div>
                <div class="eyebrow">DNS RECORDS</div>
                <h2>DNS and mail records</h2>
                <p>Monitor public address, nameserver, MX, SPF-related TXT, DKIM, and DMARC record changes.</p>
                <span class="monitor-link">See DNS monitors →</span>
            </a>
            <a class="product-card monitor-card" href="/products/website-change">
                <div class="monitor-icon">≠</div>
                <div class="eyebrow">WEBSITE CHANGE</div>
                <h2>Whole-page content changes</h2>
                <p>Store normalized webpage observations and record when the fetched content fingerprint changes.</p>
                <span class="monitor-link">See website change monitoring →</span>
            </a>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="public-section split-callout">
        <div>
            <div class="eyebrow">MY CLARITY</div>
            <h2>Everything you asked Clarity to watch.</h2>
            <p>My Clarity shows what changed recently, which follows are healthy or need attention, and the observation history Clarity has built for you.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mock-feed">
            <div><span class="badge">Changed</span><strong>Webpage content changed</strong><small>Before and after saved</small></div>
            <div><span class="badge">Recovered</span><strong>Website responding again</strong><small>4 minutes ago</small></div>
            <div><span class="badge">Reminder</span><strong>SSL expires in 14 days</strong><small>Renewal approaching</small></div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="public-section ecosystem-section">
        <div class="section-intro">
            <div class="eyebrow">HOW CLARITY FITS</div>
            <h2>Software Belongs helps you do. Clarity helps you know.</h2>
            <p>Software Belongs gives people useful tools. Clarity keeps watch over public signals that change over time. AutoPilot IT brings the same self-service philosophy to business technology.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ecosystem-grid">
            <a href="https://softwarebelongs.com"><strong>Software Belongs</strong><span>DO — useful tools that help you act.</span></a>
            <div class="ecosystem-current"><strong>Clarity Belongs</strong><span>KNOW — keep an eye on what matters.</span></div>
            <div><strong>AutoPilot IT</strong><span>HANDLE — self-service technology for business.</span></div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="public-cta">
        <div class="eyebrow">STOP CHECKING</div>
        <h2>Give Clarity a public target to keep an eye on.</h2>
        <p>Start with a website, endpoint, domain, certificate, DNS record, or public service status source. Clarity builds the history from there.</p>
        <AuthorizeView>
            <Authorized>
                <a class="button" href="/add">Watch something</a>
            </Authorized>
            <NotAuthorized>
                <a class="button" href="/signup">Start free</a>
            </NotAuthorized>
        </AuthorizeView>
    </section>
</div>
